{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_4bb6ff425a744551874d0ae5","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 2/2 files\n--- File Contents ---\n\n// File: collab/1791358000000-stream-s2c.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md (markdown)\n# S2c report: request liveness (claude-opus-5-5)\n\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2`, branch `stream-crossmachine-s2` @ `91ab84f7`, uncommitted.\n\n## Edits\n\n### `src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc`\n\n- **Policy.** `links` adds `:dao.stream.remote/give-up-after` to its policy and to the positive-integer-or-nil validation (`ex-info \"invalid DaoStream remote link policy\"`). `new-link` stores `:give-up-after` and `:now nil`.\n- **Deadline stamping.** New `new-deadline` gives `now + give-up-after`, or nil when either is missing, so a clock-less composition stamps nothing. Following the sign-off note, the deadline is set where a request first exists on the link:\n  - **Accepted sends.** `register!` now takes the deadline. `send-request!` and `refl-append` pass it on the writer's `ok`, and `send-named!` stamps it on `ok`.\n  - **Kept probes.** `send-request!`'s keep branch stores `:deadline` on the `:pending` entry. A kept probe that is later sent, or refused again, carries its pending deadline: the lookup comes first, so it is never restamped.\n  - **Waiting probes.** A probe waiting on its reflection (`:probe`, the S2b recovery path) has no deadline until `admit-probe!` gets it onto the link, where it is stamped at that moment.\n  - **Resends.** `count-ask!` never touches `:deadline`.\n  - **Answers.** An answer removes the outstanding entry, deadline included.\n- **New `link-step!`, exposed as `links`' `:step`.** It is called as `(step cd now)`.\n  - It records `:now`, then runs `drain!`, which is budgeted.\n  - Unless the channel is already gone, it takes the least id among outstanding and pending entries with `:deadline <= now`. For that id it emits `{:dao.stream.remote/event :dao.stream.remote/channel-expired :dao.stream.remote/id id :dao.stream.remote/op op}`, then runs the existing `channel-loss!`. That abandons outstanding requests, emits `append-unknown` per abandoned append, and sets `channel-gone?`.\n  - It answers `{:dao.stream.remote/channel-gone? bool :dao.stream.remote/expired id-or-nil}`, or nil for a channel this peer does not reach.\n  - After the loss, the existing paths give `transport-error` / `channel-gone` (not retryable) for `cursor`, `next` and `resolve`, while `descriptor` still answers `ok`.\n- Docstrings updated: `new-link`, `send-request!`, `links`, `attacher`.\n\n### `src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc`\n\n- `dial`'s policy `select-keys` adds `:dao.stream.remote/give-up-after`, and the docstring says so. Only the namespaced key is accepted, as in spec §1.2; there is no bare `:give-up-after` alias.\n- **`dial-step!` is now multi-arity.**\n  - `([dial] (dial-step! dial nil))`: the 1-arity hands no `now`, so the link is not stepped and nothing ever expires. Existing callers are unchanged.\n  - `([dial now])`:\n    - It records `:now` on the dial, then runs the budgeted projection.\n    - It then calls the link's `(:step! ch) (:cd ch) now` and runs the budgeted mirror.\n    - If the step answers `channel-gone? true`, it closes the ws handle (idempotent). The host then deposits `:ws/closed`, and the projection closes the ring.\n- **`establish!`** stores `:cd` and `:step!` in the channel map. When the dial has already been stepped with a `now`, it steps the new link at that `now` before the attach probe is sent.\n  - Without this, the probe `dial-attach!` sends immediately would have no deadline, since the link didn't exist at the last step. The establishment stall the spec meant to bound would then go unbounded on the dial path.\n  - A composition that never steps with `now` is unchanged.\n\n### Docs\n\n- **`dao.stream.remote.md`**\n  - §2.4 Channel loss names expiry as a cause.\n  - A new **Expiry** paragraph covers the `:step` contract and return value, the stamping rules (accepted or kept, kept probes carrying their deadline, waiting probes unstamped, resends never moving it, answers clearing it), the clock-less default, `give-up-after` as channel liveness, false loss under a flood, and the dial closing its handle.\n  - §2.5: the reflection still reads no clock, because the driver supplies `now`. `append-unknown` is also reported on expiry, and there is a UDP composition note.\n  - §3.0: a new **Request liveness** bullet.\n- **`dao.stream.ws.md`** Deferred, Liveness bullet: rewritten to point to remote §2.4 Expiry for request liveness. Probing an idle connection stays open.\n\n## Tests\n\n### `remote_test.cljc`\n\nNew fixtures: `stepped-links`, `attach-via`, `step-at`, `gone`.\n\n- **`a-request-past-its-deadline-is-channel-loss`**\n  - With give-up-after 10 and a step at 0, the probe, a `next` and an `append!` all carry deadline 10.\n  - A step at 9 changes nothing.\n  - A step at 10 answers gone with expired 0. The events are `channel-expired` (id 0, op descriptor), then `append-unknown` for the append.\n  - Outstanding is then empty. `next`, `cursor` and `resolve` answer `channel-gone`; `descriptor` answers `ok`.\n- **`a-resend-does-not-move-the-deadline`**\n  - With resend-after 1, a `next` sent at 0 is re-sent across steps at 3, 6 and 9.\n  - Its deadline stays at 10, and the step at 10 loses the channel.\n- **`an-answer-before-the-deadline-clears-it`**: the probe and a `next` are answered and drained by step 12; a step at 20 finds no loss; the filed `:a` is returned.\n- **`a-kept-probe-has-a-deadline`**\n  - The writer always answers `full`. The kept probe has deadline 10, and a refused retry at step 5 keeps it.\n  - The step at 10 expires id 0.\n- **`without-a-stepped-now-nothing-expires`**: never stepped; nothing is stamped, the channel is not gone, and the reflection keeps re-sending.\n- **`flood-cannot-defer-expiry`**: drain-budget 2 with 60 unrelated values queued; a step at 5 is not gone, and the step at 10 expires id 0.\n- **`an-invalid-give-up-after-is-a-composition-error`**: 0, -1 and 1.5.\n- **`a-step-of-an-unreached-channel-is-nil`.**\n- **`drain-budget-counts-malformed-values-and-a-gap`** (S2b follow-up)\n  - Setup: a 2-slot answer ring, so 3 values cause a gap, and drain-budget 2.\n  - The 1st drain meets the gap. The 2nd reads the two malformed values left after the gap. The 3rd reads the probe's answer.\n\n### `ws_project_test.cljc`\n\nNew fixtures: `dial-with`, `toy-cd`.\n\n- **`dial-step-with-now-closes-the-handle-on-expiry`**\n  - Step at 0, then attach; the handle is still open at 9 and closed at 10.\n  - After the host's `:ws/closed` is deposited, the projection is closed and the ring answers `closed`.\n  - `dial-resolve!` then answers `channel-gone`.\n- **`the-one-arity-dial-step-never-expires`**: give-up-after is set, and five 1-arity steps leave the handle open; resolve still answers retry.\n- **`dial-propagates-link-options`** (S2b follow-up): drain-budget, max-outstanding, max-filed and give-up-after all reach the link.\n\n## Notes for review\n\n1. `establish!` stepping the new link at the dial's last `now` is the one behavior beyond the brief's letter (rationale above). Without it, the `dial-step-with-now...` scenario only works if the first deadline-carrying request is sent after a later step.\n2. `channel-loss!` still leaves `:pending` in place after expiry. The sign-off said this is inert: `drain!` returns early once the channel is gone, and `close!` clears it. I didn't change it.\n3. The cosmetic test message \"the source's own blocked\" from the S2b round 2 is left as is. It still accurately describes the `list-stream` source answering `blocked` at its end.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `clojure -M:test -n dao.stream.remote-test -n dao.stream.ws-project-test`: Ran 83 tests containing 609 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- `mise exec -- cljstyle check` on the 4 changed source and test files: clean.\n- `clj -M:kondo --lint` on the same 4 files: errors 0, 1 warning (`remote_test.cljc:661:13 unused binding peer2`). That warning was already there.\n- Not run: `bb test:clj` and the full 3-host `bb test` (Node and Dart).\n\n\n// File: collab/1791359934597-stream-s2c-review.qwen3.8-max.findings.md (markdown)\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-07 08:08:32 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-07 15:08:32 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nCoding-Agent: cmd (qwen/qwen3.8-max)\nSession-ID: b7f3f7fd-25b6-4b50-b5a5-d072e8563a1a\n\nWrite permissions are blocked in this session too, so I can't save the file. The review is complete — here is the full report, ready to be saved to `collab/1791359934597-stream-s2c-review.qwen3.8-max.findings.md`:\n\n---\n\n# S2c review: request liveness & channel expiry (qwen3.8-max)\n\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2`, branch `stream-crossmachine-s2`, base `91ab84f7`, uncommitted changes under review: `src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc`, `src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc`, both test files, and both design docs.\n\nRead firsthand: both source files in full, the S2c test sections, `dao.stream.remote.md` §2.4 (Channel loss + Expiry), §2.5, §3.0, `dao.stream.ws.md` Deferred/Liveness, the architect spec (§1.2–§4), the S2c prompt and author report. Method note: shell and write access were blocked in this session, so `git diff` was not run; the review is against the full working-tree files, cross-checked line by line against every claim in the author report. All claimed edits and tests were located and verified.\n\n## Finding summary\n\n| # | Severity | Location | Description | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | P3 | `remote.cljc` `link-step!` (~1112–1129) | `(step cd nil)` erases a previously recorded `:now` and, once any entry carries a `:deadline`, throws on `(<= deadline nil)` on all three hosts. Unreachable via `dial-step!` (guarded by `some? now`), but `:step` is public API of `links`. | Guard `link-step!`: when `now` is nil, skip recording and skip the scan (or throw a composition error). |\n| 2 | P3 | deadline stamping; `ws_project.cljc` `establish!` | A request that first exists on the link **before any timed step never receives a deadline**, even after the driver starts stepping with `now`. The `establish!` fix covers only dials already stepped at a `now`; a driver that attaches first and steps later leaves the attach probe — the establishment stall Expiry bounds — undying. Follows the spec's letter (\"before any step with `now`, nothing is stamped\"); the spec is silent on backfill. | Record for the Architect: document that drivers must step with `now` before first attach/resolve, or amend the spec to backfill deadlines at the first timed step. Non-blocking for S2c; matters for the S3a driver. |\n| 3 | P4 | `remote.cljc` `send-named!` | `(new-deadline link)` computed twice in the `cond->`. Pure and correct under driver discipline, but fragile. | `let`-bind the deadline once. |\n| 4 | P4 | `remote.cljc` `channel-loss!` | `:pending` survives channel loss (author note 2, deliberately left). Inert per S2b sign-off, but a reflection that never closes retains its entry for the link's lifetime. | Optional hygiene: clear `:pending` in `channel-loss!`. Not required. |\n| 5 | P4 | tests | No test expires a **named** resolve request through `:step` (`send-named!`'s stamping path); only post-loss `resolve` → `channel-gone` is covered. | Add: unanswered named request, step at deadline, expiry. |\n\n## Detailed analysis\n\n**`remote.cljc` — policy.** `give-up-after` added to the `links` `select-keys` and to positive-integer-or-nil validation (`ex-info \"invalid DaoStream remote link policy\"`); `new-link` stores it plus `:now nil`. Tested with 0, −1, 1.5. Matches spec §1.2/§1.3.\n\n**`new-deadline`.** `(+ now give-up-after)`, nil when either is missing — clock-less compositions stamp nothing. Arithmetic is portable (int+int and mixed comparison are clean on JVM/CLJS/Dart; epoch-ms magnitudes are far below any precision boundary).\n\n**Stamping discipline**, verified on every path: accepted sends stamp via `register!` (`send-request!`, `refl-append`, `send-named!`); kept probes carry their original deadline because `send-request!` does the **pending lookup first** — never restamped on retry or eventual send (verified in `a-kept-probe-has-a-deadline`); waiting `:probe` entries are unstamped until `admit-probe!`; `count-ask!` touches only `:asks`, never `:deadline`; `absorb!`/`absorb-named!` remove the entry, deadline included. All exactly per spec.\n\n**`link-step!` / `:step`.** Order matches the spec: record `:now`, budgeted `drain!`, then — skipped when `channel-gone?` is already true, so an `end`-loss in the same step doesn't double-report — scan `(concat outstanding pending)` for the least id with `:deadline <= now`, emit `channel-expired` (id, op), run `channel-loss!` (abandons outstanding, `append-unknown` per append, sets gone). Return shape `{:dao.stream.remote/channel-gone? bool :dao.stream.remote/expired id-or-nil}`; nil for unreached channels. Drain-before-scan is the right ordering: an answer arriving in the deadline's own tick clears its entry before the scan. `:step` creating the link on a reached-but-unattached channel via `link-for!` is harmless and pre-records `:now`. Only gaps: findings 1–2.\n\n**Flood immunity.** The scan is independent of drain-budget; `flood-cannot-defer-expiry` (budget 2, 60 junk values) demonstrates the accepted D3 trade-off (possible false loss, never deferred expiry).\n\n**Memory.** No new leak: `:outstanding` cleared on loss; `:filed`/`:filed-cursors` bounded by `max-filed` (S2b); `:pending` retention is pre-existing and bounded by `max-outstanding` when composed (finding 4). Expired entries can't accumulate — expiry is whole-channel loss and all send paths guard on `channel-gone?`.\n\n**Portability.** No reader conditionals needed: `some->`, `concat`, `sort-by key`, numeric `<=` are clj/cljs/cljd-safe. No side effects inside `swap!` in the new paths (`emit!`/`channel-loss!` run outside swaps). The only reachable type hazard is finding 1's `(<= deadline nil)`.\n\n**`ws_project.cljc` — `dial`.** Policy `select-keys` gains `give-up-after`; namespaced-key-only per spec; `dial-propagates-link-options` verifies all four link keys land on the link atom.\n\n**`dial-step!` multi-arity.** 1-arity delegates with nil and preserves existing callers exactly (no `:now`, no link step, nothing expires — `the-one-arity-dial-step-never-expires`). 2-arity: records `:now` on the dial, budgeted projection, link step **between** projection and mirror (correct: freshly deposited answers reach the link before the expiry scan), budgeted mirror once outside any atom update (`dial-mirror-effects-run-once-per-step` still guards this), then closes the ws handle when the step answers gone — `closable?`-checked and idempotent, so repeated post-loss ticks are safe. Nil `stepped` is falsy in the gone-check — no spurious close.\n\n**`establish!`.** Stores `:cd`/`:step!` and, when the dial has a recorded `now`, steps the new link before any probe exists — since `:step` creates the link via `link-for!`, the later `:attach` reuses it with `:now` set, so the immediately-sent attach probe is stamped. This is the one beyond-the-letter behavior; the rationale is sound and the mechanism verified. Residual gap is finding 2.\n\n**Tests.** All seven required `remote_test` cases and both `ws_project_test` cases exist and assert the right things, plus the two S2b follow-ups. Highlights verified: exact event sequence in `a-request-past-its-deadline-is-channel-loss` (`channel-expired` id 0 op descriptor, then `append-unknown`), exact step return maps at 9/10, `next`/`cursor`/`resolve` → `channel-gone` not retryable, `descriptor` still `ok`; the full teardown chain in `dial-step-with-now-closes-the-handle-on-expiry` (handle open at 9, closed at 10, `:ws/closed` closes projection and ring, resolve answers `channel-gone`). Fixtures are consistent with file style. Gap: finding 5.\n\n**Docs.** §2.4 names expiry as a loss cause; the Expiry paragraph matches the implementation exactly (contract, return shape, all stamping rules, resend immobility, answer clearing, clock-less default, liveness framing, flood caveat, dial handle close). §2.5 keeps \"the reflection reads no clock\" true, adds the UDP note. §3.0 gains the Request-liveness bullet. `dao.stream.ws.md` Deferred/Liveness points at remote §2.4. No drift between doc text and code.\n\n**Author report cross-check.** Every claim located in the tree, including the three review notes. The reported runs (83 tests / 609 assertions, cljstyle clean, kondo 0 errors with the pre-existing `peer2` warning) could not be re-executed here — re-run `clojure -M:test -n dao.stream.remote-test -n dao.stream.ws-project-test` before landing.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**ACCEPT.**\n\nThe slice implements architect spec §1.2/§1.3 (S2c rows), the §2 failure table, §3 test plan and §4 doc amendments faithfully; stamping, resend immobility, answer clearing, expiry-scan ordering and dial teardown are correct and well-tested, with no portability or memory regressions. Findings 1–5 are non-blocking: 1 is a one-line robustness guard on a path the shipped composition never takes; 2 is a spec-silent ordering question for the Architect record and S3a; 3–5 are hygiene. Recommend landing as one commit (`feat(dao.stream.remote): request deadlines, channel-expired and link step (cross-machine stream slice S2c)`) after re-running the test lanes, tracking findings 1, 2 and 5 as follow-ups.\n\n---\n\nTo get this into `collab/1791359934597-stream-s2c-review.qwen3.8-max.findings.md`, re-run me with write permissions (or exit plan mode) and I'll save it.\n\n"}],"deferred":false}}
