{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_6f90a926f5a341c882feed8d","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 150 lines\nNote: showing lines 1090-1239. More of the file remains. Use offset=1240 to continue.\n1090: ;; =============================================================================\n1091: ;; The remote descriptor dispatch (2.2)\n1092: ;; =============================================================================\n1093: \n1094: (defn- valid-remote-descriptor?\n1095:   \"A remote descriptor names a stream and a channel: the generic\n1096:    envelope rules, the :dao.stream/remote type, and a channel\n1097:    descriptor. It carries no authorization, no surface and no\n1098:    anchors; the mirror answers those.\"\n1099:   [d]\n1100:   (and (stream/valid-descriptor? d)\n1101:        (= :dao.stream/remote (:dao.stream/type d))\n1102:        (contains? d :dao.stream/channel)))\n1103: \n1104: \n1105: (defn- link-step!\n1106:   \"One driver step of the link at `now`: record `now`, drain (within\n1107:    the drain budget), then, when an outstanding or kept request is\n1108:    past its deadline, emit channel-expired for the least such id and\n1109:    lose the channel (channel-loss!). The link reads no clock: `now` is\n1110:    the driver's. Answers whether the channel is gone and the id that\n1111:    expired, if any.\"\n1112:   [link now]\n1113:   (swap! link assoc :now now)\n1114:   (drain! link)\n1115:   (let [{:keys [outstanding pending channel-gone?]} @link\n1116:         overdue (when-not channel-gone?\n1117:                   (->> (concat outstanding pending)\n1118:                        (filter (fn [[_ e]]\n1119:                                  (some-> (:deadline e) (<= now))))\n1120:                        (sort-by key)\n1121:                        first))]\n1122:     (when-some [[id e] overdue]\n1123:       (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n1124:                    :dao.stream.remote/channel-expired\n1125:                    :dao.stream.remote/id id\n1126:                    :dao.stream.remote/op (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req e))})\n1127:       (channel-loss! link))\n1128:     {:dao.stream.remote/channel-gone? (:channel-gone? @link)\n1129:      :dao.stream.remote/expired (first overdue)}))\n1130: \n1131: \n1132: (defn links\n1133:   \"The asking side over one set of per-channel links: {:attach f\n1134:    :resolve g :step h}. `f` is `attacher`'s entry. `(g channel-descriptor\n1135:    name)` is the link's resolve over the link `f` keeps for that\n1136:    channel, created here when none exists yet: a filed answer for the\n1137:    name is returned and forgotten -- ok with the remote descriptor of\n1138:    the stream the name maps to, its own identity over that channel,\n1139:    and the entry's declared surface under :dao.stream.remote/surface;\n1140:    the not-found error as transport-error with reason not-found;\n1141:    otherwise the named descriptor request is sent when none is\n1142:    outstanding and the answer is transport-error with\n1143:    :dao.stream/retry? true, as cursor answers. After channel loss the\n1144:    answer is transport-error naming channel-gone. A channel this peer\n1145:    does not reach is not-found. `(h channel-descriptor now)` is the\n1146:    driver's step of that channel's link at `now` (link-step!): nil for\n1147:    a channel this peer does not reach, otherwise\n1148:    {:dao.stream.remote/channel-gone? bool :dao.stream.remote/expired\n1149:    id-or-nil}. Without a stepped `now` nothing expires. `opts` is\n1150:    `attacher`'s; a bound among them (:dao.stream.remote/drain-budget,\n1151:    max-outstanding, max-filed, give-up-after) that is neither nil nor a\n1152:    positive integer is a composition error.\"\n1153:   [opts]\n1154:   (let [channels (:dao.stream.remote/channels opts)\n1155:         policy (select-keys opts [:dao.stream.remote/events\n1156:                                   :dao.stream.remote/resend-after\n1157:                                   :dao.stream.remote/budget\n1158:                                   :dao.stream.remote/drain-budget\n1159:                                   :dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding\n1160:                                   :dao.stream.remote/max-filed\n1161:                                   :dao.stream.remote/give-up-after])\n1162:         _ (when-not (every? #(pos-int-or-nil? (get policy %))\n1163:                             [:dao.stream.remote/drain-budget\n1164:                              :dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding\n1165:                              :dao.stream.remote/max-filed\n1166:                              :dao.stream.remote/give-up-after])\n1167:             (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream remote link policy\"\n1168:                             {:policy policy})))\n1169:         by-channel (atom {})\n1170:         link-for! (fn [cd]\n1171:                     (swap! by-channel\n1172:                            (fn [m]\n1173:                              (if (contains? m cd)\n1174:                                m\n1175:                                (assoc m cd\n1176:                                       (new-link cd (get channels cd)\n1177:                                                 policy)))))\n1178:                     (get @by-channel cd))]\n1179:     {:attach\n1180:      (fn [descriptor]\n1181:        (if-not (valid-remote-descriptor? descriptor)\n1182:          (result :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor)\n1183:          (let [cd (:dao.stream/channel descriptor)]\n1184:            (if-not (contains? channels cd)\n1185:              (result :dao.stream/not-found)\n1186:              (let [link (link-for! cd)\n1187:                    refl (atom {:link link\n1188:                                :descriptor descriptor\n1189:                                :identity (:dao.stream/identity descriptor)\n1190:                                :surface nil\n1191:                                :source-descriptor nil\n1192:                                :gone? false\n1193:                                :closed? false\n1194:                                :ids #{}})]\n1195:                (send-request!\n1196:                  link refl\n1197:                  (wire-request link refl :dao.stream/descriptor []))\n1198:                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n1199:                 :dao.stream/handle (ReflectionHandle. refl)\n1200:                 :dao.stream/attachment (str (random-uuid))})))))\n1201:      :resolve\n1202:      (fn [cd n]\n1203:        (if-not (contains? channels cd)\n1204:          (result :dao.stream/not-found)\n1205:          (resolve-name (link-for! cd) n)))\n1206:      :step\n1207:      (fn [cd now]\n1208:        (when (contains? channels cd)\n1209:          (link-step! (link-for! cd) now)))}))\n1210: \n1211: \n1212: (defn attacher\n1213:   \"The composition's :dao.stream/attach entry for :dao.stream/remote\n1214:    descriptors; a dynamic dispatch table has this entry and no\n1215:    :dao.stream/create one, because attaching through this transport\n1216:    never creates. `opts` carries the composition data:\n1217:    :dao.stream.remote/channels maps each channel descriptor this peer\n1218:    reaches to its own end {:reader r :writer w} -- two ring buffers in\n1219:    one process today, the ws, udp and pair channels of section 3\n1220:    later; :dao.stream.remote/events is the optional event writer the\n1221:    links emit on; :dao.stream.remote/resend-after is the links'\n1222:    resend-after k, unbounded on an ordered reliable channel and small\n1223:    on udp; :dao.stream.remote/budget is the budget stamped on every\n1224:    next request; :dao.stream.remote/drain-budget bounds the reads per\n1225:    drain, :dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding the requests outstanding\n1226:    or kept per link, :dao.stream.remote/max-filed the filed answers\n1227:    and installed outcomes per link, and\n1228:    :dao.stream.remote/give-up-after the ms after a request's first send\n1229:    at which a driver step at `now` declares its channel lost, each nil\n1230:    for unbounded. One link is kept per channel descriptor, shared by\n1231:    every reflection through that channel. attach! answers ok at once\n1232:    with a reflection handle and a local, opaque\n1233:    :dao.stream/attachment -- the contract's deferred remote\n1234:    confirmation -- and the link sends one descriptor probe for the\n1235:    identity: its answer is the reflection's confirmation, not-found\n1236:    marking the reflection gone, ok recording the source's descriptor\n1237:    and declared surface. `links` gives the same entry with the link's\n1238:    resolve beside it.\"\n1239:   [opts]"}],"deferred":false}}
{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_dcb8abfd46fa4557a10a00dd","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 180 lines\nNote: showing lines 330-509. More of the file remains. Use offset=510 to continue.\n330:    writer has refused, kept unsent with the reflection each was sent\n331:    for; filed answers keyed by id; the more outcomes installed at\n332:    their served identity and the cursor that precedes each; an\n333:    optional event writer; and the policy data -- the resend-after k,\n334:    the budget k stamped on next requests, and the bounds on reads per\n335:    drain, on outstanding plus kept requests and on filed plus\n336:    installed answers, and the give-up-after liveness bound, all\n337:    composition data; and the last `now` a driver stepped it at.\"\n338:   [cd chan policy]\n339:   (atom {:channel cd\n340:          :reader (:reader chan)\n341:          :writer (:writer chan)\n342:          :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n343:                    (stream/cursor (:reader chan) :dao.stream/oldest))\n344:          :outstanding {}\n345:          :pending {}\n346:          :filed {}\n347:          :filed-cursors {}\n348:          :filed-seq 0\n349:          :events (:dao.stream.remote/events policy)\n350:          :resend-after (:dao.stream.remote/resend-after policy)\n351:          :budget (:dao.stream.remote/budget policy)\n352:          :drain-budget (:dao.stream.remote/drain-budget policy)\n353:          :max-outstanding (:dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding policy)\n354:          :max-filed (:dao.stream.remote/max-filed policy)\n355:          :give-up-after (:dao.stream.remote/give-up-after policy)\n356:          :now nil\n357:          :next-id 0\n358:          :channel-gone? false}))\n359: \n360: \n361: (defn- mint-id!\n362:   \"The next asker-minted id, unique per channel.\"\n363:   [link]\n364:   (let [n (:next-id @link)]\n365:     (swap! link assoc :next-id (inc n))\n366:     n))\n367: \n368: \n369: (defn- emit!\n370:   \"Append one event to the link's event writer when one is composed;\n371:    without an event writer the event is dropped.\"\n372:   [link v]\n373:   (when-some [w (:events @link)]\n374:     (stream/append! w v)))\n375: \n376: \n377: (defn- new-deadline\n378:   \"The deadline of a request that first exists on the link now: the\n379:    last stepped `now` plus give-up-after. Nil without either -- a\n380:    clock-less composition stamps nothing and nothing expires.\"\n381:   [link]\n382:   (let [{:keys [now give-up-after]} @link]\n383:     (when (and (some? now) (some? give-up-after))\n384:       (+ now give-up-after))))\n385: \n386: \n387: (defn- register!\n388:   \"Record `req` as outstanding under its id, with the request it was\n389:    sent for, its ask count, the reflection that sent it, and its\n390:    deadline when it has one.\"\n391:   [link refl req deadline]\n392:   (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)]\n393:     (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id]\n394:            (cond-> {:req req :asks 0 :reflection refl}\n395:              (some? deadline) (assoc :deadline deadline)))\n396:     (swap! refl update :ids conj id)))\n397: \n398: \n399: (defn- stamped-budget\n400:   \"The budget a next request carries: the link's budget, no more than\n401:    max-filed when both are composed -- the link could retain no more\n402:    outcomes than that, so asking for more would only be dropped.\"\n403:   [link]\n404:   (let [{:keys [budget max-filed]} @link]\n405:     (if (and (integer? budget) max-filed)\n406:       (min budget max-filed)\n407:       budget)))\n408: \n409: \n410: (defn- wire-request\n411:   \"One request map for the channel, its id asker-minted; a next\n412:    request carries the link's stamped budget when one is composed.\"\n413:   [link refl op args]\n414:   (let [k (stamped-budget link)]\n415:     (cond-> {:dao.stream/identity (:identity @refl)\n416:              :dao.stream.remote/op op\n417:              :dao.stream.remote/args args\n418:              :dao.stream.remote/id (mint-id! link)}\n419:       (and (= :dao.stream/next op) (some? k))\n420:       (assoc :dao.stream.remote/budget k))))\n421: \n422: \n423: (defn- room?\n424:   \"True when the link holds fewer than max-outstanding requests,\n425:    outstanding or kept, not counting `id` itself, or has no such bound.\n426:    Sends and kept probes are both admitted only with room, so\n427:    outstanding plus kept never exceeds the bound, and a kept probe's\n428:    own retry -- which excludes itself -- always has room.\"\n429:   [link id]\n430:   (let [{:keys [max-outstanding outstanding pending]} @link]\n431:     (or (nil? max-outstanding)\n432:         (< (+ (count outstanding) (count (dissoc pending id)))\n433:            max-outstanding))))\n434: \n435: \n436: (defn- send!\n437:   \"Append `req` to the channel writer, unless the link has no room\n438:    for it: that send is refused locally as though the writer answered\n439:    full, nothing crossing.\"\n440:   [link req]\n441:   (if (room? link (:dao.stream.remote/id req))\n442:     (stream/append! (:writer @link) req)\n443:     {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full}))\n444: \n445: \n446: (defn- send-request!\n447:   \"Append one request map to the channel writer and register it as\n448:    outstanding only when the writer accepted the send: a send the\n449:    writer refuses with full leaves the request unsent and nothing\n450:    outstanding, so the operation answers as though unanswered and the\n451:    next ask sends again. A send over max-outstanding is refused the\n452:    same way (send!). An attach descriptor probe refused with full is\n453:    kept on the link instead, unsent, one retry per drain until a send\n454:    is accepted -- when the link has room for it; otherwise it waits on\n455:    its own reflection, unadmitted, and that reflection's next operation\n456:    offers it again (admit-probe!). A request's deadline is stamped\n457:    the first moment it exists on the link, accepted or kept; a kept\n458:    probe carries its deadline into its later accepted send, and a\n459:    probe waiting on its reflection has none until admitted. Returns\n460:    the writer's outcome.\"\n461:   [link refl req]\n462:   (let [r (send! link req)\n463:         id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)\n464:         deadline (if-some [kept (get (:pending @link) id)]\n465:                    (:deadline kept)\n466:                    (new-deadline link))]\n467:     (cond\n468:       (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n469:       (do (register! link refl req deadline)\n470:           (swap! link update :pending dissoc id)\n471:           (swap! refl dissoc :probe))\n472: \n473:       (and (= :dao.stream/full (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n474:            (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op req)))\n475:       (if (room? link id)\n476:         (do (swap! link assoc-in [:pending id]\n477:                    (cond-> {:req req :reflection refl}\n478:                      (some? deadline) (assoc :deadline deadline)))\n479:             (swap! refl dissoc :probe))\n480:         (swap! refl assoc :probe req)))\n481:     r))\n482: \n483: \n484: (defn- count-ask!\n485:   \"Count one further ask of the outstanding request `id`; on reaching\n486:    the link's resend-after k, re-send it once -- the same id, a\n487:    duplicate of an idempotent operation, which recomputes the same or a\n488:    later, equally true answer -- and start counting afresh. append! is\n489:    never re-sent: it never stays outstanding beyond its send.\"\n490:   [link id]\n491:   (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n492:     (let [k (:resend-after @link)\n493:           asks (inc (:asks entry))]\n494:       (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id :asks] asks)\n495:       (when (and (integer? k) (pos? k) (<= k asks))\n496:         (stream/append! (:writer @link) (:req entry))\n497:         (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id :asks] 0)))))\n498: \n499: \n500: (defn- outstanding-for\n501:   \"The id of the link's outstanding request for `op` with `arg` sent by\n502:    `refl`, if any; the request each outstanding id was sent for makes\n503:    the correlation.\"\n504:   [link refl op arg]\n505:   (when-some [[id _]\n506:               (first\n507:                 (filter (fn [[_ e]]\n508:                           (let [r (:req e)]\n509:                             (and (= refl (:reflection e))"}],"deferred":false}}
