{"type":"event","event":{"type":"thinking_end","text":"Verified. dial-step!: projection → link-step (between projection and mirror) → mirror → close handle when gone. Note that the mirror's step is executed even after the channel has vanished — the handle is still writable, the mirror responds to peer requests; closing happens after that. Harmless.\n\nOne subtle point: when `stepped` indicates gone, the mirror has already been executed against the handle in this tick — no problem.\n\nIdempotency: the `(stream/closable? handle)` guard and close! — repeated ticks after loss: `stepped` still returns a channel-gone? true map (link-step! returns a map; the overdue scan is skipped because channel-gone? is already true — wait, no: line 1116 `when-not channel-gone?` → overdue is nil, returns {:channel-gone? true :expired nil}). Then closable? becomes false after close → no double close. Good.\n\nestablish! lines 513-514: if now has been recorded, step the new link with now before the attach probe is sent by reflect! (dial-attach! line 551). Verified.\n\nNext, check channel-loss! and drain! to confirm the loss semantics, and further verify the stamping of send-named! (line 927, lines 992-993) and refl-append. Let's look around lines 540-560 (channel-loss!), around 570-600 (drain!), and around lines 920-1000.\n"}}
