{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_d8d6b773306944fc840d8d9b","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 110 lines\nNote: showing lines 560-669. More of the file remains. Use offset=670 to continue.\n560:          :surface (conj (into #{} (:dao.stream.remote/surface answer))\n561:                         :closable)))\n562: \n563: \n564: (defn- next-age!\n565:   \"The next arrival age on the link: filed answers and installed\n566:    outcomes are aged in the order the link retained them.\"\n567:   [link]\n568:   (let [n (:filed-seq @link)]\n569:     (swap! link assoc :filed-seq (inc n))\n570:     n))\n571: \n572: \n573: (defn- evict-filed!\n574:   \"Bound the link's filed answers and installed outcomes together by\n575:    max-filed, evicting the oldest retained until within the bound. The\n576:    entry just filed is the newest, so filing an answer never evicts\n577:    that answer. Everything filed is idempotent-recomputable, so the\n578:    operation an evicted entry answered asks again; no outcome is\n579:    invented.\"\n580:   [link]\n581:   (when-some [m (:max-filed @link)]\n582:     (loop []\n583:       (let [{:keys [filed filed-cursors]} @link]\n584:         (when (< m (+ (count filed) (count filed-cursors)))\n585:           (let [aged (concat (map (fn [[id e]] [(:age e) :filed id]) filed)\n586:                              (map (fn [[k e]] [(:age e) :filed-cursors k])\n587:                                   filed-cursors))\n588:                 [_ where k] (apply min-key first aged)]\n589:             (swap! link update where dissoc k)\n590:             (recur)))))))\n591: \n592: \n593: (defn- file!\n594:   \"File answer `v` under `id` with the request it was sent for and the\n595:    reflection that sent it, as the newest retained entry, then bound\n596:    the retained entries by max-filed.\"\n597:   [link id req v refl]\n598:   (swap! link assoc-in [:filed id]\n599:          {:req req :ans v :reflection refl :age (next-age! link)})\n600:   (evict-filed! link))\n601: \n602: \n603: (defn- install-more!\n604:   \"Install each more outcome under the answer's served identity and at\n605:    the cursor that precedes it, so a later next at that cursor by a\n606:    reflection of the same stream returns the source's own outcome\n607:    without a request. The identity is half of the key: two served\n608:    identities can carry equal cursor values, and an outcome belongs to\n609:    its own stream. At most the link's stamped budget k less one are\n610:    installed -- the answer itself is the first of k -- and none when\n611:    the link stamped no budget: the surplus a peer sends is dropped.\n612:    Prefetch only fills free retained capacity: with max-filed, no more\n613:    are installed than fit beside what is already retained, so a\n614:    prefetch never evicts anything, its own answer included.\"\n615:   [link answer]\n616:   (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity answer)\n617:         k (stamped-budget link)\n618:         asked (if (and (integer? k) (pos? k)) (dec k) 0)\n619:         {:keys [max-filed filed filed-cursors]} @link\n620:         fits (if max-filed\n621:                (max 0 (- max-filed (count filed) (count filed-cursors)))\n622:                asked)]\n623:     (loop [cur (:dao.stream/cursor answer)\n624:            more (take (min asked fits) (:dao.stream.remote/more answer))]\n625:       (when (and cur (seq more))\n626:         (let [[o & further] more]\n627:           (swap! link assoc-in [:filed-cursors [identity cur]]\n628:                  {:outcome o :age (next-age! link)})\n629:           (recur (:dao.stream/cursor o) further))))))\n630: \n631: \n632: (defn- absorb-named!\n633:   \"A resolve's answer, read off the channel: taken only when it echoes\n634:    the name its outstanding request asked, and filed under its id for\n635:    the resolve that asked. No reflection exists for a name, so nothing\n636:    is marked gone and nothing is emitted. An answer that does not echo\n637:    the name never completes the request, which stays outstanding.\"\n638:   [link id entry v]\n639:   (let [req (:req entry)]\n640:     (when (and (named? v)\n641:                (= (:dao.stream.remote/name req)\n642:                   (:dao.stream.remote/name v)))\n643:       (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)\n644:       (file! link id req v nil))))\n645: \n646: \n647: (defn- absorb!\n648:   \"Consume one value read off the channel. A well-formed answer whose\n649:    id is outstanding and whose identity is the outstanding entry's\n650:    reflection's own identity is taken: a not-found error marks the\n651:    reflection gone; the attach probe's ok records the source's\n652:    descriptor and declared surface; an append!'s source outcome is\n653:    emitted on the event writer, correlated by id; any other answer is\n654:    filed under its id and its more outcomes installed. Answers whose\n655:    id is not outstanding, answers whose identity is not the\n656:    reflection's own -- a mismatch never completes a request, which\n657:    stays outstanding, and an answer that carries no identity\n658:    completes no identity request -- and values that are not\n659:    well-formed answers,\n660:    are dropped as diagnostics. The answer to a named request is the\n661:    resolve's (absorb-named!).\"\n662:   [link v]\n663:   (when (well-formed-answer? v)\n664:     (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id v)]\n665:       (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n666:         (if (named? (:req entry))\n667:           (absorb-named! link id entry v)\n668:           (let [refl (:reflection entry)\n669:                 req (:req entry)"}],"deferred":false}}
{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_225f061fe22142fab6b7bab3","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 110 lines\nNote: showing lines 900-1009. More of the file remains. Use offset=1010 to continue.\n900:             (send-or-count! link refl :dao.stream/next c)\n901:             (result :dao.stream/blocked))\n902:           (translated :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone)))))\n903: \n904: \n905: (defn- refl-append\n906:   \"The append! operation: send the request and return the channel\n907:    writer's outcome -- ok is acceptance on the outbound path, exactly\n908:    the contract's Writing rule for a transport that carries values\n909:    toward a stream elsewhere. The source's outcome is emitted on the\n910:    event writer when it is filed, correlated by id; append! never\n911:    answers the source's full. Only an accepted send is in flight: a\n912:    refused append! never crossed, so its effect is not unknown; a send\n913:    over max-outstanding answers full, nothing crossing.\"\n914:   [refl v]\n915:   (let [link (:link @refl)]\n916:     (drain! link)\n917:     (admit-probe! refl)\n918:     (cond\n919:       (:closed? @refl) (result :dao.stream/closed)\n920:       (:gone? @refl) (translated :dao.stream.remote/not-found)\n921:       (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/append!)\n922:       (translated :dao.stream.remote/no-surface)\n923:       :else\n924:       (let [req (wire-request link refl :dao.stream/append! [v])\n925:             r (send! link req)]\n926:         (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n927:           (register! link refl req (new-deadline link)))\n928:         r))))\n929: \n930: \n931: (defn- refl-close\n932:   \"The close! operation, local: the reflection forgets its\n933:    outstanding ids and its kept, unsent probe, reporting each\n934:    outstanding append! on the event writer as append-unknown -- an\n935:    append whose answer never arrives has unknown effect; afterwards\n936:    append! answers closed, cursor answers closed, next answers filed\n937:    outcomes then end, and nothing crosses the wire. Idempotent, per\n938:    the contract's Close.\"\n939:   [refl]\n940:   (let [link (:link @refl)]\n941:     (swap! link update :pending\n942:            (fn [kept]\n943:              (into {}\n944:                    (remove (fn [[_ e]]\n945:                              (= refl (:reflection e)))\n946:                            kept))))\n947:     (swap! refl dissoc :probe)\n948:     (drain! link)\n949:     (when-not (:closed? @refl)\n950:       (doseq [id (:ids @refl)]\n951:         (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n952:           (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n953:             (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n954:                          :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n955:                          :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\n956:           (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)))\n957:       (swap! refl assoc :closed? true :ids #{}))\n958:     (result :dao.stream/ok)))\n959: \n960: \n961: ;; =============================================================================\n962: ;; The link's resolve (2.4)\n963: ;; =============================================================================\n964: \n965: (defn- named-id\n966:   \"The least id in `entries` -- the link's outstanding or filed map --\n967:    whose request is a named request for the name `n`, if any.\"\n968:   [entries n]\n969:   (first\n970:     (sort\n971:       (keep (fn [[id e]]\n972:               (let [r (:req e)]\n973:                 (when (and (named? r) (= n (:dao.stream.remote/name r)))\n974:                   id)))\n975:             entries))))\n976: \n977: \n978: (defn- send-named!\n979:   \"Append one named descriptor request for `n` to the channel writer,\n980:    outstanding only when the writer accepted the send: a refused send\n981:    leaves the request unsent and the next resolve