he channel writer is the ws handle itself.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-530-`ws-project` holds the reading cursor on the attachment's traffic medium,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-531-keeps the events whose `:ws/attachment` names this channel, appends the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-532-`:ws/value` of each `:ws/payload` onto the ring buffer, and drops\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-533-`:ws/error` diagnostics. A terminal lifecycle event for the attachment\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-534-(`:ws/closed`, `:ws/ended`) or a failure resolution (`:ws/not-found`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-535-`:ws/transport-error`) makes `ws-project` close the ring buffer: channel\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-536-loss is then the link's `end` observation (2.4). `ws-project` is a step the\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-537-composition drives at its own cadence, as it drives `endpoint-step`.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-538-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-539-Direction is establishment, not authority. A WebSocket has a dialer and an\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-540-acceptor because TCP does. Once established the channel is symmetric and\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-541-nothing in this document remembers who dialed. Hosts: clj, cljs on Node and\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-542-cljd may dial or accept (`src/clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj`,\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-543-`src/cljs/dao/stream/ws/node.cljs`, `src/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd`);\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-544-cljs in a browser may only dial (`src/cljs/dao/stream/ws/browser.cljs`).\n/Users/s