irst timed step don't get a deadline, no backfill): conforms to the letter of the spec (\"nothing is stamped before a step with now\"). Ruling: document the driver's contract — the driver must step with `now` before the first attach/resolve. The dial path already enforces this via `establish!`. Backfill on the first timed step is rejected for S2c: stamping an old request with a \"now + give-up-after\" deadline at the first timed step conflates the driver's start time with the request's send time, and silently changing the deadline semantics is a spec amendment, not a follow-up. If S3a finds that real drivers cannot guarantee step-before-attach, revisit backfill as a spec amendment at that point. Accepted as an S3a follow-up, with a docs note in the S3a slice.\n- Findings 3–5 (P4 hygiene: double computation of new-deadline in send-named!, `:pending` surviving loss, no named-expiry test): non-blocking, tracked as S3a hygiene. Note finding 4 — pending entries surviving channel-loss! is indeed inert (drain! returns early when gone. Send paths guard on channel-gone? — wait, does retry-pending! run inside drain! before the gone check? No: line 747 of drain! `when-not channel-gone?` wraps everything including retry-pending!. And send-request! is called from operations… refl operations check gone? first. OK, inert).\n\n**4. Verdict:** Conditional SIGN-OFF GRANTED: rerun the test lane before landing (the reviewer couldn't run tests; the author reported 83/609 green — the signoff should require the committer to rerun), land as a single commit with the proposed message, track findings 1, 2, 5 as S3a follow-ups.\n\nNow — I'm in plan mode. I can't write to collab/. I need to write the plan file to ~/.commandcode/plans/, include the full signoff report, and set up the plan so that on approval the report is written to collab/1791360593148-architect-stream-s2c-signoff.qwen3.8-max.findings.md. Note that the task header says model qwen/qwen3.8-max, but I'm Command Code — the filename