{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Even writing the plan file is being blocked — it seems this session is running in a print mode without write permissions (same situation as the reviewer's session who was complaining that writing was blocked). The reviewer's file 1791359934597...findings.md contains a note saying \"Write permissions are blocked in this session too, so I can't save the file,\" but that file currently exists on disk (I read it from disk). In other words, someone saved it later.\n\nSince I can't write anywhere, I have to output the report within the response so the orchestrator can save it. Same as what the reviewer did. But according to git status, collab/1791360593148-architect-stream-s2c-signoff.qwen3.8-max.prompt.md and .stdout.log already exist — my standard output gets recorded to stdout.log. Therefore, the best action is: output the complete report within the response and note that it should be saved to the findings path.\n\nRegarding response format rules like conciseness — the task requires a complete report; the user is implicitly requesting details. I'll output the report.\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Write permissions are blocked in this session (both the plan file and `collab/`), so I'll deliver the complete sign-off report here for saving to `collab/1791360593148-architect-stream-s2c-signoff.qwen3.8-max.findings.md`. The review itself is complete — I verified the implementation firsthand, read-only.\n\n---\n\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-07 08:10:00 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-07 15:10:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nCoding-Agent: cmd (qwen/qwen3.8-max)\n\n# Lead System Architect: Slice S2c sign-off — request liveness and channel expiry\n\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2`, branch `stream-crossmachine-s2`, base `91ab84f7`, uncommitted S2c diff.\n\nRead firsthand for this sign-off: `remote.cljc` (`new-deadline`, `register!`, `send-request!`, `count-ask!`, `channel-lo