ing {} :channel-gone? true))\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-712-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-713-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-714-(defn- retry-pending!\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-715-  \"One more try of each probe the writer has refused, once per drain,\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-716-   until a send is accepted; the accepted send is registered as the\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-717-   outstanding probe and the normal filing path confirms it.\"\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-718-  [link]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-719-  (doseq [[_ e] (:pending @link)]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-720-    (send-request! link (:reflection e) (:req e))))\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-721-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-722-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-723-(defn- admit-probe!\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-724-  \"Offer `refl`'s unadmitted attach probe to its link again: a probe\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-725-   the link had no room to keep waits on its own reflection, so the\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-726-   link's kept state stays within max-outstanding, and is sent, kept,\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-727-   or left waiting by send-request! as on attach.\"\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-728-  [refl]\n--\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc:734:(defn- drain!\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-735-  \"Read the link's channel reader to blocked, filing each answer: the\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-736-   caller's own polling is the cadence and no driver step exists. An\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-737-   end is the channel's loss; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-738-   cursor, the lost wire values being lost. Each drain is also one\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-739-   further ask of an outstanding descriptor probe -- the probe's\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-740-   caller never asks it remotely, where a named request's caller asks\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-741-   by calling resolve again -- so resend-after re-sends it, and\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-742-   one more try of each probe the writer has refused, until a send\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-743-   is accepted. With a drain-budget, at most that many reads -- ok and\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-744-   gap alike -- are taken per drain, the link's cursor kept where it\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-745-   stopped for the next operation's drain.\"\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-746-  [link]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-747-  (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-748-    (doseq [[_ e] (:outstanding @link)]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-749-      (when (and (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req e)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-750-                 (not (named? (:req e))))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-751-        (count-ask! link (:dao.stream.remote/id (:req e)))))\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-752-    (retry-pending! link)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-753-    (loop [remaining (:drain-budget @link)]\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-754-      (when-not (and remaining (zero? remaining))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-755-        (let [r (stream/next (:reader @link) (:cursor @link))]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-756-          (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-757-            :dao.stream/ok\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-758-            (do (absorb! link (:dao.stream/value r))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-759-                (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-760-                (recur (when remaining (dec remaining))))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-761-            :dao.stream/blocked nil\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-762-            :dao.stream/end (channel-loss! link)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-763-            :dao.stream/gap\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc-764-            (do (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r)) nil)"}]},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_c53121b9587e4db180d41b81","content":[{"type":"text","text":"docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-360-**Channel loss.** A channel ends when its reader answers `end`: the\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-361-projection closed it (3.1), the pair adapter closed it on an `in` gap or\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-362-end (3.3), or the medium is gone; or a driver step finds a request past\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:363:its deadline (Expiry, below). The link then abandons its outstanding\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-364-ids and reports each\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-365-abandoned `append!` on the event writer as `append-unknown` (2.5), and\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-366-answers later `cursor` and `next` `transport-error` with\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-367-`:dao.stream.remote/reason :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone`, not retryable;\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-368-`append!` keeps answering the channel writer's own outcome, `closed` once\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-369-the channel is down. Filed answers are still returned. Reattachment is the\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-370-caller's policy, by `attach!` on the same descriptor.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-371-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:372:**Expiry.** `links` also gives `:step`, `(step channel-descriptor now)`:\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-373-the driver's step of that channel's link at `now`, nil for a channel this\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-374-peer does not reach. It records `now` on the link, drains (within the drain\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-375-budget), and then, if an outstanding or kept request has `:deadline <=\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-376-now`, appends `{:dao.stream.remote/event\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-377-:dao.stream.remote/channel-expired :dao.stream.remote/id id\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-378-:dao.stream.remote/op op}` for the least such id to the event writer and\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-379-loses the channel as above. It answers `{:dao.stream.remote/channel-gone?\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-380-bool :dao.stream.remote/expired id-or-nil}`. With\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-381-`:dao.stream.remote/give-up-after ms`, a request's deadline is the last\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-382-stepped `now` plus `ms`, stamped the first moment the request exists on\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-383-the link: its accepted send, or its keeping as a refused attach probe, a\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-384-kept probe carrying that deadline into its later send. A probe waiting on\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-385-its reflection has none until the link admits it. A resend never moves a\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-386-deadline, and an answer clears the request with its deadline. Without\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-387-`give-up-after`, or before any step with `now`, nothing is stamped and\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-388-nothing expires. `give-up-after` is a liveness statement about the channel,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-389-not the request: on an ordered reliable channel an unanswered request past\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-390-it means the peer is not serving. A flood of unrelated values cannot defer\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-391-it, because the drain budget bounds each step's reads while `now`\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-392-advances; under such a flood the loss may be false, which costs a\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-393-reattachment and invalidates nothing. Whatever owns the connection closes\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-394-it on loss: `dao.stream.ws-project`'s `dial-step!` given `now` closes its\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-395-ws handle.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-396-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-397-**Resolve.** A link also answers `resolve` `name`, for no reflection. It\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-398-drains, then returns and forgets a filed answer for the name: `ok` with\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-399-the remote descriptor of the identity answered over the link's channel,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-400-`:dao.stream/identity` and `:dao.stream.remote/surface`; or the filed\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-401-`not-found` as `transport-error` with\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-402-`:dao.stream.remote/reason :dao.stream.remote/not-found`, which marks\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-403-nothing. A filed `oversize` is returned the same way, with its own name as\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-404-the reason. Otherwise it sends the named request if none is outstanding for\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-405-the name and answers `transport-error` with `:dao.stream/retry? true`, as\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-406-`cursor` does. A send the channel writer refuses with `full` is retried by\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-407-the next `resolve`; any other refusal is returned as the writer's own\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-408-outcome, leaves nothing outstanding and is remembered nowhere, so each\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-409-`resolve` of that name attempts the send again. A named answer is filed\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-410-only when its id is outstanding and it echoes the name asked. An answer\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-411-that carries no `:dao.stream/identity` completes no identity request.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-412-After channel loss `resolve` answers `transport-error` with\n--\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-433-### 2.5 Loss and resend\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-434-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-435-The reflection reads no clock: the only time a link knows is the `now` a\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:436:driver hands its `:step` (2.4, Expiry). A link's\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-437-`:dao.stream.remote/resend-after k`\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-438-means: an outstanding `descriptor`, `cursor` or `next` request is re-sent\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-439-when the caller has asked `k` further times and it is still unanswered.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-440-`k` is unbounded on an ordered reliable channel and small on UDP. Those\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-441-three operations are idempotent, so a duplicate request recomputes the same\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-442-or a later, equally true answer. `append!` is never re-sent:\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-443-deduplication and correlation are the payload's (OD-2, accepted), and an\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-444-append whose answer never arrives has unknown effect, reported on the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-445-event writer as `{:dao.stream.remote/event :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-446-:dao.stream.remote/id n}` when the reflection is closed or the channel ends\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-447-or expires. On UDP (3.2) compose `resend-after` small and `give-up-after`\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-448-generous or nil.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-449-There are no sessions, no acknowledgement vectors, no windows and no result\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-450-retention at the answering peer: the cursor is the sequence number for\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-451-reads, and `gap` remains the source's declaration, never a channel artifact.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-452-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-453-## 3. Channels\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-454-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-455-A channel declares a portable value domain, a frame budget, and whether it\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-456-is ordered and reliable; the link reads the last as composition data for\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-457-`:dao.stream.remote/resend-after`, and nothing else in section 2 changes\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-458-per channel.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-459-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-460-### 3.0 Stepped channel composition boundary and resource bounds\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-461-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-462-`dao.stream` is the sole abstraction boundary for communication across\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-463-machine boundaries: neither higher-level interpreter runtimes (such as\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-464-`yin.repl`) nor evaluation surfaces (such as `yin.vm.linker`) know or care\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-465-about underlying transport specifics (TCP WebSocket vs UDP datagram).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-466-Swapping transport mechanisms beneath `dao.stream` preserves all handle\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-467-operations, outcome algebras, opaque cursors, source gap/recovery semantics,\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-468-and append semantics. Raw network drop or connection loss is never invented\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-469-or reported as a source-retention gap.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-470-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-471-Channel compositions are stepped and driver-paced: cadence is owned by the\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-472-composition runner, not by ambient timers, daemon loops, or background\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-473-threads. All stepped channel compositions observe an explicit resource bounds\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-474-contract:\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-475-- **Finite admission cap (`:max-sessions`)**: An accepting channel composition\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-476-  enforces an upper bound on active concurrent sessions. When `:max-sessions`\n--\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-502-- **Request liveness (`give-up-after`)**: `:dao.stream.remote/give-up-after`,\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-503-  a positive integer of milliseconds or nil, bounds how long a request may\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md-504-  stay unanswered, measured against the `now` a driver hands the link's\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.